{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "1CO",
  "chapter": 13,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, but have not love, I am become sounding brass, or a clanging cymbal.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if I have ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the gift of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " prophecy, and know all mysteries and all knowledge; and if I have all faith, so as to remove mountains, but have not love, I am nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And if I bestow all my goods to feed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the poor",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and if I give my body to be burned, but have not love, it profiteth me nothing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Love suffereth long, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is kind; love envieth not; love vaunteth not itself, is not puffed up,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "doth not behave itself unseemly, seeketh not its own, is not provoked, taketh not account of evil;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "rejoiceth not in unrighteousness, but rejoiceth with the truth;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "beareth all things, believeth all things, hopeth all things, endureth all things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Love never faileth: but whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " prophecies, they shall be done away; whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tongues, they shall cease; whether ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " knowledge, it shall be done away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For we know in part, and we prophesy in part;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "but when that which is perfect is come, that which is in part shall be done away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When I was a child, I spake as a child, I felt as a child, I thought as a child: now that I am become a man, I have put away childish things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For now we see in a mirror, darkly; but then face to face: now I know in part; but then shall I know fully even as also I was fully known.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CO.13.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:1CO.13.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now abideth faith, hope, love, these three; and the greatest of these is love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
